{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>In every place where I make mention of My name.</b> It should have said תזכיר — 'you shall make mention' — for in every place where a person makes mention of the name of the Holy One, blessed be He, in the house of prayer or in other places, there, may He be blessed, is He worshipped." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah he said אזכיר — 'I will make mention' — for this verse contains a key to understanding the matter of the sacrifices. And these verses are the speech of the special Name, and therefore it says: <b>An altar of earth you shall make for Me</b> — for Me alone, for the special Name — and you shall offer the sacrifices upon it. And in every place where I draw the will to My name by means of the sacrifices, I will come to you and bless you — thus the blessings are drawn to you from now on, for when the blessing emanates to His name from the source of blessing, then the world is blessed. And the word אזכיר is from the root of אזכרתה, which is the drawing of fragrance; as it is said (Isaiah 66), מזכיר לבונה; (Jeremiah 17) כזכור בניהם מזבחותם; (Song of Songs 1) נזכירה דודיך מיין. And the sense of אזכיר את שמי is as though it said 'I will make My name fragrant,' and its meaning is: I will draw the will to My name. And the reason he said בכל המקום — with the definite article — is to allude to the house of sacrifices, which is called 'the place,' that Solomon built for the name of the Holy One, blessed be He, as it is written (1 Kings 8) והבית אשר בניתי לשמך. And from this it did not say בכל מקום — 'in every place' — for it is impossible to offer the sacrifices in every place; and thus it is written (Deuteronomy 12:13–14) השמר לך פן תעלה עולותיך בכל מקום אשר תראה כי אם במקום אשר יבחר וגו׳."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:01:53.122116601Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}